---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'Author one step';
const subtitle = 'Write the rename rule. Run it against the fixture. See what 14 lines of authored migration feels like.';
---
<Base title={title} description={subtitle}>
  <article class="etude-page">
    <header class="etude-head">
      <p class="etude-kicker">Etude · The anti-cascader</p>
      <h1 class="etude-title">{title}</h1>
      <p class="etude-relief">{subtitle}</p>
      <nav class="etude-nav">
        <a href="/etudes/anti-cascader/">← anti-cascader etudes</a>
        <span class="etude-nav-sep">·</span>
        <a href="/puzzles/bob-the-fixer-as-anti-cascader/">essay</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <section class="etude-intro">
      <p>The codemod inside one step of the migration is not magic. It is a small pattern: <strong>match this; replace with that; constrain by where it appears.</strong></p>
      <p>You're authoring step 02 of <code>/migrate-spring-boot-3</code>. Edit the rules. Hit run. See it land against a fixture file.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="etude-stage">
      <div class="etude-card">
        <p class="etude-step">Rules · javax → jakarta</p>

        <div class="rule-presets">
          <button type="button" class="preset-btn preset-active" data-preset="starter">Starter</button>
          <button type="button" class="preset-btn" data-preset="full">Full</button>
          <button type="button" class="preset-btn" data-preset="overzealous">Overzealous</button>
          <button type="button" class="preset-btn" data-preset="empty">Empty</button>
        </div>

        <div class="rule-editor">
          <div class="rule-grid" id="rule-grid"></div>
          <button type="button" id="add-rule" class="rule-add">+ add rule</button>
        </div>

        <div class="rule-actions">
          <button type="button" id="run" class="etude-next">Run rules against fixture</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="etude-card">
        <p class="etude-step">Fixture · <code>OrderEntity.java</code></p>
        <p class="fixture-help">Same file, before and after. Diff highlighted in green and red.</p>
        <div class="fixture-grid">
          <div class="fixture-col">
            <p class="fixture-col-name">Before</p>
            <pre class="fixture-code" id="fixture-before"></pre>
          </div>
          <div class="fixture-col">
            <p class="fixture-col-name">After</p>
            <pre class="fixture-code" id="fixture-after">(run rules to see)</pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="etude-card">
        <p class="etude-step">Assertions · what should be true</p>
        <ul class="assert-list" id="assert-list"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="etude-failure">
      <h2 class="etude-failure-title">What just happened</h2>
      <p>You wrote a transform. You ran it against a fixture. You saw assertions pass or fail. <strong>That's the loop a migration author lives in.</strong> Not 700 lines of LLM-generated refactor; a small set of mechanical rules with a fixture corpus that shows when you got too greedy or too conservative.</p>
      <p>Bob's contribution isn't this rule shape — codemod engines have shipped this for years. Bob's contribution is the <em>wrapper</em>: the explanation that prints before this rule runs, the per-step PR cadence, the state file. The rule itself is the boring deterministic core.</p>
    </section>

    <footer class="etude-coda">
      <p>14-line transforms. 14-line PRs. Each one reviewable. Each one teachable.</p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Base>

<script is:inline>
  // Tiny string-based codemod runner. The fixture is a Java file; rules are
  // (find-prefix, replace-prefix) pairs that match `import <find>...;` lines.
  // The runner is intentionally simple — this is not a real AST tool — so the
  // reader can see how each rule maps to a transformed line.

  const FIXTURE = [
    'package com.example.orders;',
    '',
    'import javax.persistence.Entity;',
    'import javax.persistence.Id;',
    'import javax.persistence.Column;',
    'import javax.validation.constraints.NotBlank;',
    'import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;',
    'import javax.crypto.Cipher;',
    'import javax.naming.InitialContext;',
    'import java.util.List;',
    '',
    '@Entity',
    'public class OrderEntity {',
    '    @Id',
    '    private Long id;',
    '    @Column @NotBlank',
    '    private String sku;',
    '}'
  ].join('\n');

  // The truth: which import lines should be rewritten.
  // True = should rewrite to jakarta. False = should stay on javax.
  const TRUTH = {
    'javax.persistence.Entity':         { newPkg: 'jakarta.persistence', shouldRewrite: true  },
    'javax.persistence.Id':             { newPkg: 'jakarta.persistence', shouldRewrite: true  },
    'javax.persistence.Column':         { newPkg: 'jakarta.persistence', shouldRewrite: true  },
    'javax.validation.constraints.NotBlank': { newPkg: 'jakarta.validation.constraints', shouldRewrite: true  },
    'javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest': { newPkg: 'jakarta.servlet.http', shouldRewrite: true  },
    'javax.crypto.Cipher':              { newPkg: null,                  shouldRewrite: false },
    'javax.naming.InitialContext':      { newPkg: null,                  shouldRewrite: false },
    'java.util.List':                   { newPkg: null,                  shouldRewrite: false },
  };

  const PRESETS = {
    starter: [
      { find: 'javax.persistence', replace: 'jakarta.persistence' }
    ],
    full: [
      { find: 'javax.persistence', replace: 'jakarta.persistence' },
      { find: 'javax.servlet',     replace: 'jakarta.servlet' },
      { find: 'javax.validation',  replace: 'jakarta.validation' },
      { find: 'javax.annotation',  replace: 'jakarta.annotation' }
    ],
    overzealous: [
      { find: 'javax', replace: 'jakarta' }
    ],
    empty: []
  };

  let rules = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(PRESETS.starter));

  const grid = document.getElementById('rule-grid');
  const addBtn = document.getElementById('add-rule');
  const runBtn = document.getElementById('run');
  const beforeEl = document.getElementById('fixture-before');
  const afterEl = document.getElementById('fixture-after');
  const assertList = document.getElementById('assert-list');
  const presetBtns = document.querySelectorAll('.preset-btn');

  function renderRules() {
    grid.innerHTML = '';
    if (rules.length === 0) {
      const empty = document.createElement('p');
      empty.className = 'rule-empty';
      empty.textContent = 'No rules. Add one or pick a preset.';
      grid.appendChild(empty);
      return;
    }
    rules.forEach((r, i) => {
      const row = document.createElement('div');
      row.className = 'rule-row';
      row.innerHTML = `
        <div class="rule-cell">
          <span class="rule-cell-label">Find prefix</span>
          <input type="text" class="rule-input" data-i="${i}" data-k="find" value="${escapeAttr(r.find)}" spellcheck="false" />
        </div>
        <span class="rule-arrow">→</span>
        <div class="rule-cell">
          <span class="rule-cell-label">Replace with</span>
          <input type="text" class="rule-input" data-i="${i}" data-k="replace" value="${escapeAttr(r.replace)}" spellcheck="false" />
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="rule-del" data-i="${i}" aria-label="Delete rule">×</button>
      `;
      grid.appendChild(row);
    });
    grid.querySelectorAll('.rule-input').forEach(inp => {
      inp.addEventListener('input', () => {
        const i = parseInt(inp.dataset.i, 10);
        const k = inp.dataset.k;
        rules[i][k] = inp.value;
      });
    });
    grid.querySelectorAll('.rule-del').forEach(btn => {
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const i = parseInt(btn.dataset.i, 10);
        rules.splice(i, 1);
        renderRules();
      });
    });
  }

  function escapeAttr(s) { return String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g, c => ({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c])); }
  function escapeHtml(s) { return String(s).replace(/[&<>]/g, c => ({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;'}[c])); }

  function applyRules(line) {
    // Sort longest-prefix first so a more specific rule wins over a generic one.
    const sorted = rules.slice().filter(r => r.find).sort((a, b) => b.find.length - a.find.length);
    for (const r of sorted) {
      // Match against `import <find>` (with a dot or whitespace boundary after).
      const pat = new RegExp('^(\\s*import\\s+)' + r.find.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, '\\$&') + '(\\b)');
      if (pat.test(line)) {
        return line.replace(pat, '$1' + r.replace + '$2');
      }
    }
    return line;
  }

  function renderBefore() {
    const html = FIXTURE.split('\n').map(line => {
      const isImport = /^\s*import\s+/.test(line);
      const cls = isImport ? 'fc-line fc-line-import' : 'fc-line';
      return `<span class="${cls}">${escapeHtml(line) || ' '}</span>`;
    }).join('\n');
    beforeEl.innerHTML = html;
  }

  function run() {
    const lines = FIXTURE.split('\n');
    const transformed = lines.map(line => {
      const out = applyRules(line);
      const changed = out !== line;
      return { line: out, originalLine: line, changed };
    });

    afterEl.innerHTML = transformed.map(t => {
      const cls = t.changed ? 'fc-line fc-line-changed' : 'fc-line';
      return `<span class="${cls}">${escapeHtml(t.line) || ' '}</span>`;
    }).join('\n');

    runAssertions(transformed);
  }

  function runAssertions(transformed) {
    const assertions = Object.entries(TRUTH).map(([fqcn, t]) => {
      const importLine = `import ${fqcn};`;
      const idx = transformed.findIndex(x => x.originalLine.trim() === importLine);
      const out = idx >= 0 ? transformed[idx].line.trim() : null;
      const wasRewritten = out !== null && out !== importLine;

      let pass = false;
      let actual = '';
      let expected = '';
      let label = '';

      if (t.shouldRewrite) {
        const expectedLine = `import ${t.newPkg}.${fqcn.split('.').pop()};`;
        pass = out === expectedLine;
        actual = out || '(line missing)';
        expected = expectedLine;
        label = `<code>${fqcn}</code> → <code>${t.newPkg}.${fqcn.split('.').pop()}</code>`;
      } else {
        pass = out === importLine;
        actual = out || '(line missing)';
        expected = importLine;
        label = `<code>${fqcn}</code> stays on javax`;
      }
      return { label, pass, actual, expected, fqcn, shouldRewrite: t.shouldRewrite, wasRewritten };
    });

    const passed = assertions.filter(a => a.pass).length;
    const total = assertions.length;
    const overzealous = assertions.filter(a => !a.shouldRewrite && a.wasRewritten);
    const missed = assertions.filter(a => a.shouldRewrite && !a.wasRewritten);

    let summary = '';
    if (passed === total) {
      summary = `<div class="assert-summary assert-summary-good"><strong>${passed}/${total} pass.</strong> The fixture transforms correctly. The four in-scope namespaces are rewritten; <code>javax.crypto</code>, <code>javax.naming</code>, and <code>java.util</code> are left alone.</div>`;
    } else if (overzealous.length > 0 && missed.length === 0) {
      summary = `<div class="assert-summary assert-summary-bad"><strong>${passed}/${total} pass — too greedy.</strong> Your rule rewrote ${overzealous.length} import${overzealous.length>1?'s':''} that should have stayed on javax. <code>javax.crypto</code>, <code>javax.naming</code>, and <code>javax.sql</code> are still on javax in Spring Boot 3.</div>`;
    } else if (missed.length > 0 && overzealous.length === 0) {
      summary = `<div class="assert-summary assert-summary-bad"><strong>${passed}/${total} pass — too conservative.</strong> You missed ${missed.length} namespace${missed.length>1?'s':''}. The full migration covers persistence, servlet, validation, and annotation.</div>`;
    } else {
      summary = `<div class="assert-summary assert-summary-bad"><strong>${passed}/${total} pass.</strong> Mix of misses and over-rewrites — re-check which prefixes are in scope.</div>`;
    }

    const rows = assertions.map(a => `
      <li class="assert-item assert-${a.pass ? 'pass' : 'fail'}">
        <span class="assert-mark">${a.pass ? '✓' : '✗'}</span>
        <span class="assert-body">
          <span class="assert-label">${a.label}</span>
          ${!a.pass ? `<span class="assert-detail">expected <code>${escapeHtml(a.expected)}</code><br/>got <code>${escapeHtml(a.actual)}</code></span>` : ''}
        </span>
      </li>
    `).join('');

    assertList.innerHTML = summary + `<div class="assert-rows-wrap"><ul class="assert-rows">${rows}</ul></div>`;
  }

  addBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    rules.push({ find: 'javax.', replace: 'jakarta.' });
    renderRules();
  });

  runBtn.addEventListener('click', run);

  presetBtns.forEach(b => {
    b.addEventListener('click', () => {
      presetBtns.forEach(o => o.classList.toggle('preset-active', o === b));
      rules = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(PRESETS[b.dataset.preset]));
      renderRules();
    });
  });

  renderBefore();
  renderRules();
</script>

<style is:global>
  .etude-page { max-width: 38rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0; }
  .etude-head { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .etude-kicker {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: var(--label-size);
    letter-spacing: var(--label-tracking);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .etude-title { font-family: var(--serif-display); font-size: 2.25rem; line-height: 1.15; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .etude-relief { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  .etude-nav { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .etude-nav a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; }
  .etude-nav a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .etude-nav-sep { margin: 0 0.5rem; opacity: 0.5; }

  .etude-intro { margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  .etude-intro p { margin: 0 0 0.85rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .etude-intro code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.35rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .etude-stage { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.2rem; }
  .etude-card {
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 1.25rem;
  }
  .etude-card code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.35rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .etude-step {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: var(--label-size);
    letter-spacing: var(--label-tracking);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
  }

  /* === presets === */
  .rule-presets {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
  }
  .preset-btn {
    appearance: none; -webkit-appearance: none;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 0.32rem 0.7rem;
    min-height: 32px;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: border-color 180ms ease, background 180ms ease, color 180ms ease;
  }
  .preset-btn:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .preset-btn.preset-active {
    background: var(--accent);
    border-color: var(--accent);
    color: var(--bg);
  }

  /* === rule editor === */
  .rule-editor {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.85rem 0.95rem 1rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .rule-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }
  .rule-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-items: end;
  }
  .rule-cell {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.2rem;
  }
  .rule-cell-label {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .rule-input {
    appearance: none; -webkit-appearance: none;
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.55rem;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 5px;
    color: var(--text);
    min-height: 36px;
    width: 100%;
    transition: border-color 180ms ease;
  }
  .rule-input:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--bg);
  }
  .rule-arrow {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    color: var(--muted);
    padding-bottom: 0.55rem;
  }
  .rule-del {
    appearance: none; -webkit-appearance: none;
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--muted);
    border-radius: 5px;
    width: 1.85rem;
    height: 1.85rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 0.05rem;
    transition: border-color 180ms ease, color 180ms ease;
  }
  .rule-del:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }

  .rule-add {
    appearance: none; -webkit-appearance: none;
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px dashed var(--line);
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: border-color 180ms ease, color 180ms ease;
  }
  .rule-add:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }
  .rule-empty {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
  }

  .rule-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }
  .etude-next {
    appearance: none; -webkit-appearance: none;
    font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.65rem 1.2rem; min-height: 44px;
    border: none; background: var(--text); color: var(--bg);
    border-radius: 6px; cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 180ms ease, transform 120ms ease;
  }
  .etude-next:hover { background: var(--accent); }
  .etude-next:active { transform: scale(0.97); }
  .etude-next::after { content: ' →'; }

  /* === fixture === */
  .fixture-help {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .fixture-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0.7rem;
  }
  .fixture-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .fixture-col-name {
    margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .fixture-code {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text);
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-break: break-all;
    overflow-x: auto;
    min-height: 18rem;
  }
  .fc-line { display: block; padding: 0 0.15rem; border-radius: 2px; }
  .fc-line-import { color: var(--text); }
  .fc-line-changed { background: rgba(45, 122, 62, 0.10); color: #1a5a2e; }

  /* === assertions === */
  .assert-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0; margin: 0;
  }
  .assert-summary {
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--bg);
    border-radius: 6px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
  }
  .assert-summary-good { border-left-color: #2d7a3e; background: rgba(45, 122, 62, 0.06); }
  .assert-summary-bad  { border-left-color: var(--accent); background: rgba(138, 52, 32, 0.06); }
  .assert-summary code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .assert-rows-wrap { margin: 0; }
  .assert-rows {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0; margin: 0;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  .assert-item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.25rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 5px;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .assert-mark {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .assert-pass .assert-mark { color: #2d7a3e; }
  .assert-fail .assert-mark { color: var(--accent); }
  .assert-pass { border-left: 3px solid #2d7a3e; }
  .assert-fail { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); }
  .assert-body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.2rem; }
  .assert-label { color: var(--text); }
  .assert-label code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .assert-detail {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .assert-detail code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  /* === failure / coda === */
  .etude-failure { margin: 2.5rem 0 0; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .etude-failure-title {
    font-family: var(--serif-display); font-size: 1.35rem; line-height: 1.25;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem; letter-spacing: -0.005em; color: var(--text);
  }
  .etude-failure p { margin: 0 0 0.85rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text); }
